[Music]  red andrews is known for being Archie's  dad but there's so much more to him than  meets the eye  sure he's a father but he's also a proud  member of the Riverdale community and a  hero in every sense of the word much  like everyone else in the show Fred went  through a serious character evolution  that rendered him even greater than  before  keep watching to see Fred Andrews  complete transformation he won't believe  how many differences there are between  the comics and the TV series Archie is a  comic book series that closely follows  The Adventures of teenagers Archie  Andrews Betty Cooper Veronica Lodge and  Jughead Jones this comic book has been  popular since the early 40s and has  continued to appeal to various  generations with hundreds of issues to  choose from fans of the series have  never had to scramble for new content so  when the CW was approached with the idea  of turning this legendary comic book  series into a TV show they immediately  got to work although many characters  were added to the franchise to create a  steady reality other characters were  revamped completely one of them being  Fred Andrews in the TV series were used  to seeing Betty and jugheads parents  however the comic books only showcase  parental figures like Fred and Mary  Andrews and Hyrum Lodge although fred  was present in both the comics and the  show his character underwent a huge  makeover he was given a fresh outlook  and a brand new family life and here's  where things get interesting while fred  is described as a super chill dad who's  always there for a son I meant your  music teacher last night yeah mrs.  Grundy this isn't exactly the case for  his comic book counterpart where as Luke  Perry's character was a construction  company owner comic book Fred is a  businessman who works in the automotive  industry  the original Frederick Andrews has  trouble seeing eye-to-eye with the  younger generation due to being  incredibly old-fashioned in fact some  might even describe Archie's dad as  bothered and conservative but this isn't  to say that Fred isn't a good father or  loving husband although he might have  trouble connecting with his sons Jenna  raishin that doesn't stop him from  trying he loves Archie more than  anything and the pair are quite close in  fact Fred and Archie are often seen  joking around in the comic book series  despite Fred's usual serious demeanor  underneath his cool calm and collected  exterior is a man with an extremely soft  heart and many of us were happy to see  that this last part was highlighted  throughout the TV series although the TV  series stayed true to the Archie  Duckhead Betty Ann Veronica's comic book  look the same can't be said about Fred's  because well they look nothing alike  like many comic book characters  Frederick is typically seen in the same  outfit which consists of tan dress pants  a white undershirt and a blue vest with  a vertical yellow design on it mr.  Andrews is also on the plump side and  has a hard time losing weight much to  his wife's dismay Fred is often seen  eating eggs and toasts and drinking  coffee in the comic book series as this  happens to be his favorite meal in  addition Fred's hair is black and thin  which is a very different hairdo than  the one New Age fans are used to in the  comics Fred's hair is thinning out and  is barely hanging on to the sides of his  head he's got a big and shiny bald head  that makes him look like the typical car  salesman he is for obvious reasons  Archie's dad isn't as present in the  comic books as he is in the TV series  but when he does show up he never fails  to teach Archaea valuable lesson despite  working as a businessman Fred likes to  brag about having many other skills  while he might work in a mid-level  management position  Fred feels as though he's not living up  to his full potential which is why he  wants to encourage his son to shoot for  the stars despite having some extra  weight on his frame Fred isn't someone  you want to mess with  in fact the character is known for  bragging about his strength and is said  to be stronger and more resourceful than  Archie himself in the comic books Fred  and Mary Andrews are happily married and  are often seen side-by-side however  money is tight and fred is typically  showcased trying to pinch every penny  that comes his way  [Music]  the comic book version of Fred Andrews  didn't receive a backstory so we were  delighted when Riverdale's Fred spoke  out about his upbringing Fred stories  and flashbacks helped us form a deeper  connection with his character quickly  turning him into a fan favorite much  like Archie fred was born and raised in  Riverdale where he attended the local  high school fred was best friends with  fp' Jones and ended up dating Hermione  Lodge for a short amount of time as a  teenager he was a talented baseball  player who also had a knack for music so  all in all Archie is every bit his  father's son Fred and f.p Jones formed a  band called the Fred heads in high  school which got them in in with the  ladies despite wanting to pursue a  professional career in either music or  sports  Fred's world came crashing down in his  junior year Fred's dad arty Andrews  unexpectedly passed away causing his son  to feel compelled to take over his  construction business Fred never got to  say goodbye to his dad which is  something we'll discuss at the end of  this video  Fred Andrews is a level-headed man who  always knows what to say to cheer up a  somber situation he's always a very  giving person which was clearly  showcased in season one when Fred gave  FP a construction job despite his better  judgement fred has a lot of pride which  he uses to perfect his work ethic  he's also an honourable man despite  having made some ethical mistakes  throughout the first season Fred chose  to give up his dreams to honor his  father's memory  he took over his construction business  and worked hard to maintain its revenue  after his father's passing  Fred met and married Mary after high  school and the couple soon had their  first and only son Archie unfortunately  there was trouble in paradise and mr.  and mrs. Andrews had a hard time being  in the same room together the tension  was so bad that Mary eventually moved  out of their family home to start a new  life in Chicago it's easy to see that  human Fred and cartoon Fred are two very  different people  unlike the comic book character fred is  a very attractive man who has a cool  demeanor about him the late Luke Perry  portrayed Fred Andrews on the CW TV  series Luke had always been known for  his stellar acting skills and solid  looks in fact he was once deemed as one  of the best-looking actors of his  generation so instead of having a  bulging guts thinning hair and a wacky  fashion sense fred was portrayed as a  middle-aged man with a muscular body and  a full head of brown hair on top of that  fred also had a full beard brown eyes in  a very casual wardrobe he was often seen  wearing flannel button-ups jeans and an  undershirt he stood at 5:10 and  regularly wore boots due to spending  most of his time on construction sites  on all Luke was the perfect person to  play Archie's dad in fact many people  believe that these two characters look a  lot alike  and one look at a side-by-side  comparison of the actors in their youth  is all we need to see to agree Fred had  a lot on his plate during the first  season of Riverdale not only with  Andrews construction coming up short in  the payroll departments but Archie was  seriously starting to act out Fred  quickly realized that his son was  sneaking out of the house and getting  into trouble so after seeing him with a  black eye he sat Archie down for a talk  despite having a love for music himself  Fred wasn't too supportive of Archie's  musical endeavors at first but after  seeing him play he chose to soundproof  the garage and stand by Archie's  decision everything became even more  complicated when his old flame Hermione  Lodge moved back into town on top of  that  Jason blossom had just been found dead  and a murder mystery was dividing  Riverdale things only seemed to get  worse when Alice Cooper told Fred that  Archie was sleeping with his teacher  miss Grundy on top of that Fred soon  found out the real reason Archie was  having trouble sleeping at night which  was due to having heard the gunshot that  allegedly killed Jason by Sweetwater  River by the end of season 1 Fred would  be fighting for his life after being  shot by the black hood at pop shop but  however extremely events of season 1 had  been this was only the beginning of  Fred's troubles  [Music]  Riverdale's first season ended with a  bang and many of us were desperate to  find out if Fred Andrews was going to  make it out alive although it was soon  confirmed that Fred would be regaining  consciousness fans couldn't help but  notice how much his near-death  experience changed him after undergoing  surgery fred was unable to breathe on  his own so he slipped into an  unconscious state where he battled some  of his inner demons it's here that we  got to see what Fred was really all  about instead of thinking about the  dreams he never accomplished or Hermione  Lodge Fred's subconscious revolved  around the only thing that really  mattered to him his son Archie he dreamt  of Archie's graduation day and we  showcased filming the events with a  happy Mary by his side throughout the  dream he kept repeating that he never  thought he'd get to witness his sons  graduation ceremony and sadly these  lines would later come back to haunt him  I think I'd love to see this day during  Fred's slumber he imagined the biggest  events in his son's life he pictured  Archie buy-in Veronica a ring and  proposing on top of that Fred got to  witness Archie and Veronica's wedding  day however his reverie was soon  interrupted by the black hood who tried  to take a shot at Archie these events  caused Fred to wake up he was greeted by  Archie who vowed to protect him from  that moment on however Fred revealed  that he'd only come back to protect  Archie not the other way around  Fred's near-death experience caused him  and married to grow closer together  whereas they used to have trouble being  in the same room they found comfort in  each other's presence although they  didn't get back together their entire  dynamic shifted in the right direction  The Andrews soon found out that miss  Grundy had been murdered and moose and  midge had been attacked in the woods  this said Archie to think that these  murders were connected but Fred was  skeptical of his son's beliefs Fred  began to realize that his son was his  own person and could formulate opinions  of his own so despite keeping a watchful  eye on Archie Fred learned to loosen his  grip on a son and respect his intuition  throughout the second season of  Riverdale we saw a major shift in Fred's  personality with the black hood still at  large it was only normal for Fred to be  frightened however nothing scared him  more  than his sons dedication to catch the  black hood and get his revenge  around this time Fred also began working  with the lodges and trying to improve  River Del's current situation  the lodges plan to flip the Southside  tearing it into a luxurious Eden and  while fred was on board at first he soon  began to see the truth  Hiram's arrival put an immediate end to  Fred and Hermione's relationship still  they had a very flirtatious way of  dealing with each other as the  jingle-jangle threat became more serious  Fred began to suspects that the  Southside wasn't the problem the lodges  were quick to state that the black hood  originated from the south side causing  an even bigger rift between the town  with FP &amp; gell Fred took a bigger  interest in Jughead and warned Archie to  do the same  Fred's fatherly roots obviously extended  to his pals son and he was ready to bite  the bullet to guarantee his well-being  one of Fred's biggest challenges has  always had to do with finances and his  lifelong issue was brought to a whole  new level after receiving an eighty-six  thousand dollar bill from the hospital  at first Fred believed the drastic  amount to be a mistake but soon found it  to be factual unable to pay for his  house his company and the hospital bill  Fred's nerves began to get the best of  him luckily an angel donation was made  to his cause clearing his hefty debt  problem was the lodges had been behind  this donation which amplified Fred's  dealings with the crooked family to make  matters worse the FBI began poking their  heads into Fred's business demanding his  files for the last seven years after  things between the Andrews and the  lodges became too shady for his liking  Fred made the decision to separate ties  with the family breaking his so Dell  agreement in the process although Fred  had looks the other way many times  throughout the second season he ended it  in a righteous way instead of working  with sketchy people Fred chose to run  for mayor with hopes of changing  Riverdale for the better unfortunately  he would soon be bested by the lodges as  Hermione became their and Hyrum framed  Archie for murder although he'd meet a  dead end  Fred wasn't done fighting just yet  [Music]  Fred Andrews his third and final season  proved to be the most challenging one of  all not only was he forced to watch his  son get berated by a corrupted lawyer  but he was made to watch as the lodges  turned Riverdale into a crime infested  town despite being powerless against the  jury's verdict fred was still a powerful  man so when Hiram taunted his family  during the trial he didn't hesitate to  punch him in the face watching his son  lose his freedom was the hardest thing  Fred ever had to do and he blamed  himself for the events that led up to  the trial however Archie was quick to  explain that siding with Hyrum / Fred  was his own doing and that no one was to  blame but himself  despite Archie's imprisonments Fred  remains a hopeful man who is proud to be  an alleged murderers father in season 3  we finally get to see what Fred was like  in high school and we soon find out that  Archie's dad had some secrets of his own  as the youth in Riverdale becomes  infatuated with Griffin's and gargoyles  it's soon revealed that Fred was a  member of the Midnight Club as Riverdale  falls deeper and deeper into the  gargoyle Kings clutches Fred desperately  tries to free Archie from jail but  Archie soon escapes and explains to his  father that he can't return to Riverdale  it's here that Fred learns to let go and  respect Archie's wishes however he  doesn't want Archie to be alone so when  he finds out that Archie and Jughead her  visiting GLaDOS he drives up to see  Archie and gives him Vegas for moral  support although this may seem like a  small gesture it's actually huge  considering the dog is who helps Fred  with his own loneliness as many of you  know actor Luke Perry tragically passed  away on March 4th 2019 he last appear in  the episode chapter 50 American Dreams  in a twist of fate Archie will be losing  his father at 17 years old which was how  old Fred was when his own father passed  despite dreaming of watching his son  graduate and walked down the aisle this  is no longer possible Fred drastically  evolved in three short seasons he went  from being extra Stern to understanding  and a little crooked to righteous he  never lost hope in his son and was  always ready to lend a helping hand Luke  Perry's abroad  passing has devastated fans and loved  ones and many are curious to see if  Riverdale will honor his memory and  according to Cole Sprouse who plays  Jughead a few episodes have been  dedicated in his honor so what do you  guys think about Fred's evolution let us  know how you feel about the character in  the comments below and be sure to drop  some kind words about the late great  Luke Perry while you're at it give this  video a big thumbs up if you love river  del and don't forget to hit that  subscribe button for more character  evolutions like the swim thanks for  watching and see you next time  [Music]

